# Serializer vectors the HTML serializer does not pass, one per line:
#
#   <file>#<n>[:xhtml] TAB <kind> TAB <reason> TAB <digest>
#
# The id is the file in third_party/html/html5lib-tests/serializer and the vector's position in it, from 1, with
# `:xhtml` for the variant written as XHTML. The kind is `standard` (the vector expects something other than the
# standard's algorithm gives; the reason quotes the served sentence, 2026-10-12) or `vocabulary` (the vector depends
# on a table of html5lib's that the standard does not have). The digest locks what this serializer produces, so a
# different failure of the same vector is a stale entry and not a hidden one.
# tools/conformance/html_serializer_suite.py fails the gate on a vector that fails and is not listed, on a listed one
# that passes or fails otherwise, and on an entry for nothing.
#
# The standard is the default. html5lib's options are a superset of it, and these seven are the places where its
# vectors ask for something the standard does not say.

